@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* NavigationShell: the frame every screen is drawn in.

   Two elements and nothing between them - the navigation and the screen - because the scaffold's
   third, an empty white bar across the top of the content, said nothing and took a row of a phone's
   screen to say it. The account actions it was built to hold live in the navigation's own pinned
   foot instead, where the design puts them.

   The grid is `dt-shell` and the screen's surface is `dt-main`, both published in `_theme.scss`
   rather than in this component's own stylesheet. That is not a filing preference: NavMenu renders
   the column on the left of this grid, so a scoped rule written here would be stamped with this
   component's scope attribute and match nothing at all.

   The connection dock sits outside the shell rather than inside it: it is fixed to the viewport and
   belongs to the circuit rather than to any screen, and a circuit failure has to be able to show
   itself over whatever the layout happens to be rendering. *@

<div class="dt-shell">
    <NavMenu />

    <main class="dt-main">
        @* FR-13: every screen's failures pass through the one boundary. *@
        <SessionExpiryBoundary>
            @Body
        </SessionExpiryBoundary>
    </main>
</div>

<DtConnectionDock />
